        "evidence": "The chart title and axes support the encoding of bars as monthly sales. The y-axis increases upward. The dashed line is labeled 'Average'. The June bar is below this line. The condition 'If this workflow routes below-average monthly sales to the low-sales response' is an assumption. The public task instructions do not explicitly state this mapping. They just say 'choose the June route'. However, the option labels are 'Route June to above-average sales bonus response', 'Route June to low-sales response', and 'Keep June on normal sales monitoring'. The term 'low-sales response' is an option. The reading checks if the chart supports the *premise* (June is below average) and notes the *conclusion* (select low-sales) depends on a workflow rule. The reading is a conditional statement. The chart supports the antecedent (June is below average). The consequent (select low-sales) depends on the workflow rule which is not explicitly defined in the text, making the final action conditional on that rule.",
